                <pb facs="0352" n="208" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg208"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-18T14:00:00+08:00">July 18, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 18—10:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>584. My 583[bis], July 17, midnight. Following from American Consul at Harbin:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 16, noon. Soviet ultimatum published here by Japanese news agency
                            last evening. Yesterday afternoon Chinese authorities closed and took
                            over railway’s four libraries here. Arriving passengers report
                            mobilization Soviet troops at Irkutsk and Chita.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
